# Jobs that need the office's files, run in the opencode container or, in host mode, by systemd
# user timers. Each line is a five-field cron expression (or @daily and the like) and a command run
# from the office root; times are UTC. A job whose last scheduled time passed while the computer was
# off runs once when the container next starts, or when systemd next runs. Run `office up` after
# changing this file.

# Update the read-only references every morning.
0 6 * * * cron/update-references.sh

# Bump the exact pins in the office's mise.toml files to versions at least a day old, and commit.
30 6 * * * cron/upgrade-tools.sh
